# The same verbs on the native surface — both surfaces are debuggable, so
# a script that only ever ran on .ink would prove nothing here.
#
# Breaks on the line AFTER the declaration: a local is only live once its
# declaring line has executed, so breaking on `let count = 3` itself would
# correctly show nothing and make a weaker fixture.
break story.brink:3
run
expect-line 3
locals
expect-local count = 3
continue
